      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14227574/assets/dff61f08e09f21935f616788e54dfb56e0d0a89f38cce9fbc6dc7333d21ba5f1.png)\n\nThe scatter plot above gives the correspondence between the variables $x$ and $y$ for some data points.\nUse the trend line to predict the value of $x$ when $y=80.$",
      "worked_solution": "To make our prediction, we proceed as follows:\n\n- First, we start at $y=80$ on the $y$-axis.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14227574/assets/e5923b6c9f0ac4dcf2aee35e67877c425b44f81830bb9f0865c5e21acf81e3f4.png)\n\n- Then, we move right until we intersect the trend line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14227574/assets/16204bd0b06918b47ae59dbd577f4fe661bbeb3d833226a0ed17dd22d1295118.png)\n\n- Finally, we move down until we intersect the $x$-axis.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14227574/assets/ba638582874f0bd353f93e8ecd56fd0e1e7445bf43b6475e86b5b2b3e4e62f97.png)\n\nTherefore, when $y=80,$ we obtain $x≈15.$",
