    "q-133932": {
      "dom_id": "step-q133932",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14227574/assets/31932ff71e679d32ba3abee0276f7a039e5f204649e63feffeb13029eabc5b88.png)\n\nAn ice cream shop wants to determine the relationship between the outside temperature $x$ (in degrees Celsius) and the number of customers $y$ they serve. The scatter plot above shows the information they collected over several days. The equation of the trend line is $y=2.25x-19.$\n\nEstimate the outside temperature if they served $53$ customers.",
      "worked_solution": "To predict the outside temperature knowing that they served $53$ customers, we need to substitute $y=53$ into the equation of the trend line and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =2.25x-19 \\\\ 53 & =2.25x-19 \\\\ 2.25x & =72 \\\\ x & =32\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, according to this model, the outside temperature is approximately ${32}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}.$\n\nNote: The point where $y=53$ is not shown on our trend line. Therefore, our result *may* be unreliable.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
