    "q-133882": {
      "dom_id": "step-q133882",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14227574/assets/6eb063fffcfd0464cbd8cf79811d9ed2ae1e820a30ec621f50e0cc3b9e150e35.png)\n\nThe scatter plot above gives the correspondence between the variables $x$ and $y$ for some data points.\nThe equation of the trend line is $y=5-0.25x.$ Assuming this trend continues, estimate the value of $y$ when $x=10.$",
      "worked_solution": "We can estimate the required value by substituting $x=10$ into the equation of the trend line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =5-0.25x \\\\  & =5-0.25(10) \\\\  & =5-2.5 \\\\  & =2.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, according to this model, when $x=10,$ we have $y≈2.5.$\n\nNote: The point where $x=10$ is not shown on our trend line. Therefore, our result *may* be unreliable.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
