    "q-133851": {
      "dom_id": "step-q133851",
      "name": "Question 10",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14227574/assets/8fb46d101101d3d2bdb4afcfcc1436f1a62137389db2ffc3fde0cff71054e7f1.png)\n\nThe scatter plot above gives the correspondence between the variables $x$ and $y$ for some data points.\nThe equation of the trend line is $y=27-0.5x.$ Assuming this trend continues, estimate the value of $y$ when $x=16.$",
      "worked_solution": "We can estimate the required value by substituting $x=16$ into the equation of the trend line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =27-0.5x \\\\  & =27-0.5(16) \\\\  & =27-8 \\\\  & =19\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, according to this model, when $x=16,$ we have $y≈19.$\n\nNote: The point where $x=16$ is not shown on our trend line. Therefore, our result *may* be unreliable.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
